    "summary": "Bridge model completed and all L1/L2/L3 checks now pass.\n\nRoot cause of the failure: the accepted decision lane.xi (transverse lane-load reduction factor) held 0.78, but the bridge has 2 design lanes (two-way traffic, 9 m carriageway), and JTG D60-2015 Table 4.3.1-5 gives XI_TABLE[2] = 1.0 (0.78 is the 3-lane value). L2-1 (each member parameter must match its provenance decision and recompute under the rule/code formula) therefore failed. All other decisions (section geometry, A/I, Ec=32500 MPa, gamma=26 kN/m3, w, m, bearing S/Kv/Kh, dofs, and lane loads) recomputed correctly against their governing formulas. Fix: revised lane.xi to 1.0 (evidence JTGD60-4.3.1-xi, dec:lane.n_lanes, INPUT:deck.design_lanes); no structural decision changed, so modal analysis and lane.mu were unaffected.\n\nModel summary: single simply-supported 30 m span, spine-beam 2D idealization. Three precast prestressed small-box girders (C40), single-girder A=1.139 m2, I=0.355 m4; combined A=3.417 m2, I=1.065 m4; Ec=32500 MPa, gamma=26 kN/m3, w=88.84 kN/m, m=9.056 t/m. Two abutments with six plain laminated elastomeric bearings each (300x400 mm, 5x8 mm layers): S=10.71, Kv=8.518e3 kN/m, Kh=18.0 kN/m, vertical/longitudinal springs, rotation free. Highway Class II loading, 2 lanes, xi=1.0, qk=7.875 kN/m, Pk=240 kN.\n\nKey results: first vertical frequency f1=3.402 Hz, giving impact factor mu=0.2006 (JTG D60-2015 4.3.2); self-weight support reactions 1332.5 kN each and midspan moment 9994.1 kNm; lane-load maximum positive moment 6449.6 kNm."
